      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Rapid progress in the understanding and treatment of unstable angina and acute coronary syndrome are prompting occasional revisions to current treatment guidelines. The recommendations contained in this paper are based on the consensus reached during discussions at the 'International Cardiology Forum' in September 1998. Consensus was reached on significant major points, although some aspects remain controversial. A substantial body of data accumulated in a host of studies justify changes to current treatment habits."},
